# Keep the benchmark's own answer key out of the corpus AFT indexes.
#
# fixtures.json, identifier-fusion-fixtures.json, baseline.json and the result
# reports each contain every fixture's query AND its expected_top_files, so
# indexing them turns a fixture query into a self-fulfilling exact hit: the
# answer-key file crowds the top of the list and pushes down the file the
# fixture is actually looking for. That deflates the measured baseline, which
# is the dangerous direction -- it makes every candidate ranking change look
# better than it is.
#
# run-fusion-quality already excludes these files from its bench-only
# exact-match oracle for the same reason. This applies the same exclusion to
# the index of the system under measurement.
#
# Patterns are relative to this directory, as in .gitignore. The .alfonso/
# reports that quote fixture queries sit above it and are already excluded by
# the repository .gitignore, which AFT's walker honors.
baseline.json
external-fixtures.json
fixtures.json
identifier-fusion-fixtures.json
prefrontal-search-fixtures.json
real-query-baseline.json
results/
